{{!
    @template theme_atrium/palette_result_body

    The inside of one palette result: icon, label and context. Shared by the link a place
    is rendered as and the button a command is rendered as, so that the two cannot drift.

    The item is a flex row with a gap, so the whitespace between these elements does not
    render.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * label - What the result is called
    * icon - A Font Awesome class, or empty for a plain dot
    * meta - A second piece of context, or empty

    Example context (json):
    {
        "label": "Course settings",
        "icon": "fa-gear",
        "meta": "Course administration"
    }
}}
{{#icon}}
    <i class="fa {{ icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
{{/icon}}
{{^icon}}
    <span class="atrium-palette-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
{{/icon}}
<span class="atrium-palette-label">{{ label }}</span>
{{#meta}}
    <span class="atrium-palette-meta">{{ meta }}</span>
{{/meta}}
